course: dictionary
lesson: 6115
title: Tiny amounts and micrograms
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some things weigh so little that grams are far too big to measure them. A microgram is a unit of mass, a way of measuring how heavy something is, for tiny amounts. «UK advice is that everyone should think about taking 10 micrograms of vitamin D a day in autumn and winter.» The word micro is a clue: it means very small.
explain: A gram is already a small unit. A milligram is a thousand times smaller than a gram, and a microgram is a thousand times smaller again. So one microgram is one millionth of a gram.
explain: Context helps you here too. «...when there isn't enough sunshine for the skin to make it.» The sentence tells you vitamin D is needed in small amounts, so it is measured in micrograms. Check by swapping in your meaning: "10 millionths of a gram of vitamin D a day" still makes sense.
fact: A microgram is a unit of mass equal to one millionth of a gram.
fact: Its symbol is µg, and medicine labels sometimes write mcg instead.
fact: 1 gram = 1000 milligrams = 1 000 000 micrograms.
fact: «Micrograms of vitamin D» measure very tiny amounts that the body needs.
fact: Micro means very small, so a microgram is much smaller than a gram.
exercise: What is a microgram? | A unit of length, like a metre | A unit of mass equal to one thousand grams | A unit of time, like a second | *A unit of mass equal to one millionth of a gram
exercise: «UK advice is that everyone should think about taking 10 micrograms of vitamin D a day.» What does micrograms tell you about the amount? | It is a time of day | *It is a tiny amount | It is a number of people | It is a very large amount
exercise: How many micrograms are in one gram? | 10 | 1 000 | *1 000 000 | 100
test: How many milligrams are in one gram? | 1 000 000 | 100 | 10 | *1000
test: What does µg mean on a label? | A milligram of salt | A gram of food | A kilogram of sugar | *A microgram
exam: Which amount is the smallest? | 1 gram | *1 microgram | 1 milligram | 1 kilogram
